{"user":"sasenchal","message":"Symmetries under observation\n\nhttps://substack.com/profile/45219856-brent-borgers/note/c-331124053?r=4buhca&utm_medium=ios&utm_source=notes-share-action\n\nmonster group c.197k dimensions to spin and make a symmetry without hitting itself (minimum dim it needs to be rotated in) encodes a fundamental Fourier coefficient - a mathematical object that has enormous causal power in our world (essentially compressing that information to this single no. The j-invariant)\n\nIn obs theory this an object in the M domain (a high dimensional space with no associativety for us ie we can't imagine it)\n\nWhat we sample is in the world of its 5-d cousin - the J invariant and the second order 4d impacts of that constant (it impacts the outcome of scientific equations, ie physics)","timestamp":"2026-09-06T19:34:57.452000+00:00","channel":"✡️⛩️samsenchal-log","channel_id":"discord:1399048923708002394","thread":null,"thread_id":null,"reply_to":null,"id":"discord:1546242322394521721","user_id":"discord:1250084478152478773","is_bot":false,"url":"https://discord.com/channels/1344300408893345863/1399048923708002394/1546242322394521721","attachments":[],"platform":"discord","server":"ORI (est. 2025)","server_id":"discord:1344300408893345863"}
