{"user":"Omar Shehata","message":"@O_oNevermore the mark of a rationalist vs post rationalist is believing in \"aesthetics contain information\"\n\nIn other words, as @Ματταθίας said to me in person the other day, \"ad hominem is not a logical fallacy. The fact that you react differently based on who said it, or _how_ someone said it, is because you are reacting to different information, not noise\"\n\nThe additional question I'd like to propose here is: when does the intuitive mind update?\n\n(like, the rational mind updates on new, logical information or deduction. But the heart / intuition does not update that way. What _does_ trigger it to update? Can you articulate precisely that mechanism?)","timestamp":"2026-09-08T16:31:08.685000+00:00","channel":"✍️eval-log","channel_id":"discord:1409673828673523762","thread":null,"thread_id":null,"reply_to":null,"id":"discord:1546920840124309614","user_id":"discord:228707291317141504","is_bot":false,"url":"https://discord.com/channels/1344300408893345863/1409673828673523762/1546920840124309614","attachments":[],"platform":"discord","server":"ORI (est. 2025)","server_id":"discord:1344300408893345863"}
